-- Café Stecker: import the real menu into the local stecker database.
-- Source: Stecker_Cafe_Menu (1).xlsx, Menu sheet, rows 2-116.
-- Prepared: 2026-10-14. Run this entire file in pgAdmin Query Tool.
-- Required menu_items columns: name, description, price, category, available,
--                             subcategory, size_volume, notes.
--
-- This script adds 107 complete product entries: 74 Getränke, 14 Speisen,
-- and 19 Eis & Desserts. IDs are generated by PostgreSQL.
-- Imported entries initially have available=true; the sheet has no stock status.
-- Existing records, including the three sample products, are retained.
-- A second run skips matching entries. It does not update existing prices.
-- Match identity: category, subcategory, name, description, size_volume.
-- Sizes and descriptions distinguish the water and sandwich variants.
--
-- Source mapping:
-- Category -> category; Subcategory -> subcategory; Item -> name;
-- Details -> description; Size/Volume -> size_volume; Price (EUR) -> price;
-- Notes -> notes. Empty source cells stay NULL.
-- Notes additionally carry the shared tea wording and the decaf surcharge.
-- Source footnote definitions are appended when their symbols are referenced.
-- Question marks and uncertain source wording are retained for later review.
--
-- Non-product rows:
-- Row 19 is a 0.20 EUR decaf surcharge. It is added to coffee notes rather
-- than inserted as a separately purchasable product.
-- Row 29 is the shared tea information. It is added to the glass-tea notes.
-- Rows 112-116 contain this footnote legend:
-- ¹ Konservierungsstoff
-- ² Farbstoff
-- ³ Antioxidationsmittel
-- ⁴ kakaohaltige Fettglasur
-- ⁵ saisonabhängig
--
-- Pending source detail:
-- Row 111 lists Milchmixgetränke at 7.50 EUR, but its individual drinks are
-- missing from the source photo. It is withheld until the details are supplied.
--
-- With the three currently confirmed samples and no other existing products,
-- the first run gives 110 database rows. The final query shows category counts.

